{"artifacts":{"sha256:235e625ea0678751/p4/tab-i":{"artifact":"table","caption":"Equilibrium Compositions and Tie-Lines of Various Phases Measured by the EPMA in the Present Work from the Fe-Mo-Ti Diffusion Couple Annealed at 1000 ~ for 480 Hours*","label":"I","page":4}},"contexts":{"doi:10.1007/bf02648587":{"context_id":"context:source-doi-10-1007-bf02648587","items":[{"applies_to":"One of the diffusion couples after annealing","extraction_accepted":false,"id":"ORC-3AL4PJUELJ","method":"XRD analysis","page":1,"quote":"One of the diffusion couples after annealing was purposely broken along the interface between different metals, and the various phases formed in the diffusion area were examined by XRD analysis.","second_reader_agrees":false,"type":"measurement"},{"applies_to":"Another diffusion couple","extraction_accepted":false,"id":"ORC-BQNL2SU63K","method":"metallographic observation and scanning electronic microscopy (SEM)","page":2,"quote":"Another diffusion couple was ground and polished and then examined through metallographic observation and scanning electronic microscopy (SEM) in order to identify interfaces between the different phases.","second_reader_agrees":false,"type":"measurement"},{"calibration":"The Camebax-Micro set was often calibrated by measuring the pure metals to ascertain that the working condition for the EPMA remains stable during the measurement.","extraction_accepted":true,"has_dropped_fields":true,"id":"ORC-2Y2AH2I5PC","instrument":"CamebaxMicro set made in France","method":"EPMA","page":3,"quote":"The present EPMA was carried out with a CamebaxMicro set made in France, and accelerating voltage was set to 15 kV. The pure metals far from the diffusion area in the specimen were chosen as Fe, Mo, and Ti standards. The measured X-ray intensity for each element was corrected and then converted into its concentration by a computer program. The Camebax-Micro set was often calibrated by measuring the pure metals to ascertain that the working condition for the EPMA remains stable during the measurement.","second_reader_agrees":true,"type":"measurement"},{"extraction_accepted":false,"has_dropped_fields":true,"id":"ORC-WZ3GWSIY3O","label":"diffusion couples of the ternary Fe-Mo-Ti system","nominal_composition":"Fe-Mo-Ti","page":1,"quote":"The starting materials used in the present work were pure iron (Fe > 99.9 wt pct), pure molybdenum (Mo > 99.5 wt pct), and pure titanium (Ti > 99.5 wt pct). Metal Ti was cut into 6 • 12 x 15 mm, whereas Fe and Mo were cut into 6 x 6 x 15 mm. In a similar technique used in a previous w o r k , 161 the diffusion couples of the ternary Fe-Mo-Ti system were prepared by tying the three different metal pieces together using pure Mo wire, as illustrated in Figure 3. In order to obtain good contact among different metals in the diffusion couples, each metal piece was ground flat before tying.","second_reader_agrees":false,"starting_materials":"pure iron (Fe > 99.9 wt pct), pure molybdenum (Mo > 99.5 wt pct), and pure titanium (Ti > 99.5 wt pct)","synthesis":"In a similar technique used in a previous w o r k , 161 the diffusion couples of the ternary Fe-Mo-Ti system were prepared by tying the three different metal pieces together using pure Mo wire, as illustrated in Figure 3. In order to obtain good contact among different metals in the diffusion couples, each metal piece was ground flat before tying.","type":"sample"},{"atmosphere_or_container":"sealed in a silica capsule under vacuum (0.0133 Pa)","cooling":"air-cooled by breaking the capsule","duration":"480 hours","duration_parsed":{"hours":480.0,"printed":"480 hours"},"extraction_accepted":true,"has_dropped_fields":true,"id":"ORC-GRB6O72DRL","page":1,"purpose":"heat treated","quote":"These specimens sealed in a silica capsule under vacuum (0.0133 Pa) were heat treated at 1000 ~ for 480 hours, during which the temperature was controlled within -+2 ~ Splitting of the diffusion couples had been encountered after water quenching. He